1
00:05:32,307 --> 00:05:38,307
A masterpiece of modern horror.

2
00:11:04,615 --> 00:11:10,615
The Shining is a horror, thriller film directed by Stanley Kubrick.

3
00:16:36,923 --> 00:16:42,923
Jack Torrance accepts a caretaker job at the Overlook Hotel, where he, along with his wife Wendy
and their son Danny, must live isolated from the rest of the world for the winter.

4
00:22:09,230 --> 00:22:15,230
But they aren't prepared for the madness that lurks within.

5
00:27:41,538 --> 00:27:47,538
Jack Torrance, played by Jack Nicholson.

6
00:33:13,846 --> 00:33:19,846
Wendy Torrance, played by Shelley Duvall.

7
00:38:46,153 --> 00:38:52,153
Danny, played by Danny Lloyd.

8
00:44:18,461 --> 00:44:24,461
Hallorann, played by Scatman Crothers.

9
00:49:50,769 --> 00:49:56,769
Ullman, played by Barry Nelson.

10
00:55:23,076 --> 00:55:29,076
Grady, played by Philip Stone.

11
01:00:55,384 --> 01:01:01,384
The Shining is a 1980 psychological horror film produced and directed by
Stanley Kubrick and co-written with novelist Diane Johnson.

12
01:06:27,692 --> 01:06:33,692
It is based on Stephen King's 1977 novel and stars Jack Nicholson,
Shelley Duvall, Danny Lloyd and Scatman Crothers.

13
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film presents the descent into insanity of a recovering alcoholic and aspiring novelist who takes a
job as winter caretaker for a mountain resort hotel with his wife and clairvoyant son.

14
01:17:32,307 --> 01:17:38,307
Production took place almost exclusively in England at EMI
Elstree Studios, with sets based on real locations.

15
01:23:04,615 --> 01:23:10,615
Kubrick often worked with a small crew, which allowed him to do many
takes, sometimes to the exhaustion of the actors and staff.

16
01:28:36,923 --> 01:28:42,923
The then-new Steadicam mount was used to shoot several scenes, giving
the film an innovative and immersive look and feel.

17
01:34:09,230 --> 01:34:15,230
The film was released in the United States on May 23, 1980, by Warner Bros., and in the United
Kingdom on October 2 by Columbia Pictures through Columbia-EMI-Warner Distributors.

18
01:39:41,538 --> 01:39:47,538
There were several versions for theatrical releases, each of which was cut
shorter than the preceding cut; about 27 minutes was cut in total.

19
01:45:13,846 --> 01:45:19,846
Reactions to the film at the time of its release were mixed; King
criticized the film due to its deviations from the novel.

20
01:50:46,153 --> 01:50:52,153
The film received two controversial nominations at the 1st Golden Raspberry Awards in 1981—Worst Director and Worst
Actress—the latter of which was later rescinded in 2022 due to Kubrick's alleged treatment of Duvall on set.

21
01:56:18,461 --> 01:56:24,461
The Shining has since been critically reappraised and is often
cited as one of the best horror films ever made.

22
02:01:50,769 --> 02:01:56,769
It was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the Library of
Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant" in 2018.

23
02:07:23,076 --> 02:07:29,076
A sequel titled Doctor Sleep, based on King's 2013 novel of the
same name, was adapted to film and released in 2019.

24
02:12:55,384 --> 02:13:01,384
The film explores themes of hotel, new year's eve, child
abuse, based on novel or book, isolation.

25
02:18:27,692 --> 02:18:33,692
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
